messages:
marta: Quick heads-up — PR #4821 has a couple of mismatches in the /v1/generate streaming examples that are confusing folks. The JS streaming snippet uses the wrong param casing and the response example omits the content payload.
ishan: @marta thanks for the ping :eyes: Which param casing do we want in the raw API examples? runtime expects snake_case in request JSON but SDKs show camelCase, right?
prashant: Correct — hosted API expects snake_case in request bodies (max_new_tokens). SDKs expose camelCase (maxNewTokens). Docs examples that show raw JSON should use snake_case.
ryan: Also noticed the response example in the streaming sample only had message.role and no content. For structured output we need something like message.content: [{"type":"output_text","text":"..."}]. That causes confusion for parser snippets.
olivia: I'll take the JS and curl snippets and update the OpenAPI examples referenced in the PR. Assigning to @olivia. I'll also add a short migration note about SDK vs API naming.
marta: Posting the minimal fix I sketched below. Incorrect JS snippet from PR:

```js
// incorrect (from PR)
fetch('/v1/generate', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'redwood-1',
    prompt: 'Hello',
    maxNewTokens: 64  // shown in PR but raw API expects snake_case
  })
})
```

Corrected raw-API example we should show in docs (use snake_case):

```js
// corrected (raw API body)
fetch('/v1/generate', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'redwood-1',
    prompt: 'Hello',
    max_new_tokens: 64,
    stream: true
  })
})

// SSE parsing (streaming) — include content in each message chunk
const es = new EventSource('/v1/streaming-endpoint');
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  const event = JSON.parse(e.data);
  // event.message should contain role and content array
  // example: { message: { role: 'assistant', content: [{ type: 'output_text', text: 'Hi' }] } }
  console.log(event.message.content[0].text);
};
```

ishan: The response example in the OpenAPI file also needs to be updated. The current example has `message.role` only which made a bunch of downstream snippets break when people copy/paste.
prashant: I'll correct the OpenAPI example in /openapi/generated.yml to include a realistic content array. If you want, I can open a tiny follow-up PR to update any generated SDK example caching that picks up the example.
ryan: Please also update the curl snippet in the same page (so docs across languages are consistent). I'll add a unit test that validates the OpenAPI example shape against our schema to avoid regressions.
doc-bot: CI: docs-lint passed, linkcheck passed for deploy-preview-4821 (preview available)
olivia: Merged the example fixes into the branch and pushed an updated deploy preview: https://staging-docs.redwood.ai/preview/4821 — changed raw JSON to use snake_case and updated streaming response samples. :shipit:
marta: Thanks everyone. I'll add a one-line note in the changelog about clarifying API vs SDK param naming and the streaming response shape. Closing the loop.
